course: dictionary
lesson: 11733
title: Avow: saying it openly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To avow something is to say it openly and firmly, so everyone can hear it. Avow is a formal word, so you will meet it more in old stories and exam texts than in everyday chat. «Mia avowed that she would never tell a lie again.» Mia is making a firm, open promise.
explain: Avow can also mean to admit something openly. «The thief avowed his crime in front of the judge.» He did not hide it or deny it. He owned up to it in public, and the words in front of the judge are the clue.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Avow is often followed by that, or by a feeling like love. «Tom avowed his love for the dog he had found.» Try the swap check: put "said openly" in place of avowed. Does the sentence still make sense? Yes, so you have the meaning.
explain: The adjective avowed appears in phrases like «an avowed enemy» and «his avowed aim». An avowed enemy is someone who has openly said they are against you. Avowed means openly declared, so everyone knows about the feeling or aim.
fact: Avow is a formal verb meaning to say something openly and firmly.
fact: Avow can also mean to admit or confess something openly.
fact: «Avowed» is an adjective meaning openly declared, as in «an avowed enemy».
fact: Avow, avows, avowed and avowing are all forms of the same word.
fact: Avow is more formal than say, so you will often find it in serious or old-fashioned writing.
exercise: «The knight avowed that he would protect the village.» What does avowed mean here? | Whispered quietly | Hid in a cave | Forgot all about it | *Said openly and firmly
exercise: «The thief avowed his crime in front of the judge.» What does avowed mean here? | Hid | *Admitted openly | Forgot | Denied it quietly
exercise: «She was an avowed fan of football.» What does avowed tell you about her? | She has never seen a game | *Her love of football is open, and everyone knows it | She is secretly afraid of football | She is a referee
test: «He avowed his love for his little sister.» What does avowed mean? | *Openly declared his love | Forgot his love | Sang a song about her | Hid it from everyone
test: «The avowed aim of the club is to help animals.» What does avowed mean? | Hidden from everyone | Something the club forgot | Not important at all | *Stated openly, so everyone knows the aim
exam: Which sentence uses avow to mean say openly? | The dog avowed under the table | *The princess avowed she would always tell the truth | Avow the sandwich quickly | The rain avowed gently on the roof
